# Valgrind suppressions for the valgrind job in native-checks.yaml.
#
# Two entries, neither zupix's: one is the qoi package's, one R's.
#
# The qoi package's: qoi 0.1.0's
# qoiRead_() keeps the buffer qoi_decode() mallocs and never frees it. The
# test suite calls qoi::readQOI() as a differential oracle for
# pix_read() (test-shapes.R, "qoi::readQOI() agrees exactly"), which is what
# provokes it.
#
# R's: do_memCompress() (src/main/connections.c) allocates a libdeflate
# compressor and keeps it in a static for reuse, never freeing it; valgrind
# sees only an interior pointer to it at exit, so it is "possibly lost".
# The test helper make_png() (helper-images.R) builds PNGs with
# memCompress(type = "gzip"), which is what provokes it.
#
# Each is matched on its whole call path, so a real leak from any other
# caller, zupix's own code included, is still reported.
{
   qoi-0.1.0-qoiRead-never-frees-qoi_decode-buffer
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite
   fun:malloc
   fun:qoi_decode
   fun:qoiRead_
}
{
   R-memCompress-keeps-its-libdeflate-compressor
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible
   fun:malloc
   fun:libdeflate_alloc_compressor_ex
   fun:do_memCompress
}
